# Step 015 — IMPLEMENT

```step
anchor: IMPLEMENT
touches: [Berreman, BerremanTests, OpticalConstructor.Domain, OpticalConstructor.Tests]
depends_on: []
```

**How to implement.** Make the transcendental dispersion models first-class in a dispersive segment. In Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs add a third EpsAxisDispersion case (Dispersion.fs:306) representing an evaluated-directly model: it carries a WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex closure exactly as the engine's own EpsWithDisp case does in this file (Dispersion.fs:11-12), and its complexIndex returns that closure applied to w. Because a function-typed union case removes F# structural equality type-wide, mark EpsAxisDispersion [<CustomEquality; NoComparison>] with equality that compares RealNK / ComplexEps structurally and the evaluated case by closure reference, so DispersionModel, EpsWithDispValue and MaterialComplexity keep the equality the existing Assert.Equal(model, back) and Assert.Equal(Ok axis, toEpsAxis model) tests use (OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349). In OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs make toEpsAxis (DispersionModels.fs:605) lower the four transcendental models TaucLorentz / GaussianOscillator / ForouhiBloomer / BrendelBormann (currently Error NotAFiniteTermSum at :666-673) to the new evaluated case via DispersionModels.evaluate (:486); toEpsAxis becomes total (all ten models lower), so remove the now-unreachable EpsAxisLoweringError / NotAFiniteTermSum (:505) and simplify toEpsValue / toOpticalProperties (:700,716). In OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs drop lowerAxis's error mapping and the SegmentNotLowerable case (:132,634,637) so toComplexity (:699) builds a dispersive segment for a transcendental model, and add a modelParameters arm for the evaluated case returning no editable term scalars. Update the four tests that asserted Error NotAFiniteTermSum (DispersionModelsTests.fs:331,377,540) and the Assert.Equal(Ok axis, toEpsAxis model) shape (:349) to the total outcome. Tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests: for each of the four models the lowered EpsAxisDispersion.complexIndex equals DispersionModels.evaluate across a sampled wavelength grid within tolerance, and a MaterialComplexity carrying a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without SegmentNotLowerable.

**Acceptance.** After the step, toEpsAxis MUST lower all ten models (the four transcendental to the evaluated case), the four NotAFiniteTermSum errors and SegmentNotLowerable MUST no longer exist, and a transcendental dispersive segment's complexIndex MUST match DispersionModels.evaluate across a sampled grid within tolerance while building through toComplexity.
